TITLE:: Stammer
summary:: a beat repeat with chance, pitch fall, decay, reverse and a filter on the repeats, as a UGen and as an object, with a window
categories:: Libraries>Stammer
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/StammerView, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
It catches a slice of what is playing and repeats it, falling, fading or backwards - a beat repeat, running anywhere a UGen does, with a window.

code::
Ndef(\drums, { Stammer.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.002, 0.1) * WhiteNoise.ar(0.4 ! 2), \stammer) }).play;

b = Stammer(Ndef(\drums), \stammer);
b.gui;
b.bpm = 140; b.grid = '1/32'; b.chance = 0.5;
b.pitchFall = 1;                  // each repeat a semitone lower
b.repeatNow;                      // go, now
b.resync;                         // the bar starts here
::

Every code::interval:: it decides, by code::chance::, whether to go, code::offset:: sixteenths into it. If it goes, it takes the last code::grid:: of sound and plays it over and over for code::hold:: sixteenths. Each repeat keeps code::decay:: of the level of the one before and falls code::pitchFall:: semitones (a negative number rises), code::reverse:: says how many slices run backwards, and code::gridVary:: changes the slice's length each time it goes. The repeats have a band filter of their own.

code::mode:: says what happens to the input: code::mix:: carries on under the repeats, code::insert:: is replaced by them while they last, and code::gate:: is only ever the repeats.

It counts its own bars at code::bpm::. Tell it the tempo and call code::resync:: on the beat to line it up with something else. It does not read Tidal's clock or anyone else's, and it will drift from a clock that is not exactly its tempo. The window has both as buttons, code::go now:: and code::resync::.

subsection:: The object and the UGen
It is an link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, so everything that class documents works here: code::Stammer.ar(in, name)::, code::Stammer(node, name)::, code::Stammer.onBus(bus, numChannels)::, presets, the clipboard, code::gui::. Its window's display is a link::Classes/StammerView::.

subsection:: Parameters
Each is a property of the object: read it, set it. The numbers are in the order of the node's control, which is what saved node maps carry. Internal ones without a knob, if any, are described above.

table::
## strong::parameter:: || strong::range:: || strong::default:: || strong::what it does::
## code::bpm:: || 20 .. 300 bpm || 120 || the tempo it counts in
## code::interval:: || 1/2 1 bar 2 bars 4 bars 1/4 || 1 bar || how often it decides whether to go
## code::offset:: || 0 .. 15 16ths || 0 || how far into that it goes, in sixteenths
## code::chance:: || 0 .. 1 || 1 || how likely it is to go when it comes round
## code::hold:: || 1 .. 32 16ths || 4 || how long it goes on, in sixteenths
## code::mode:: || mix insert gate || insert || mix: the input carries on under the repeats; insert: they replace it; gate: only ever the repeats
## code::grid:: || 1/4 1/8 1/8t 1/16 1/16t 1/32 1/32t 1/64 || 1/16 || how long a slice it takes
## code::gridVary:: || 0 .. 3 oct || 0 || how far a slice's length may stray each time it goes
## code::decay:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.9 || how much of the level each repeat keeps
## code::pitchFall:: || -12 .. 12 st || 0 || how far each repeat falls in pitch - under 0, how far it rises
## code::reverse:: || 0 .. 1 || 0 || how many slices play backwards
## code::filterOn:: || on / off || false || the band filter on the repeats
## code::filterFreq:: || 40 .. 16000 Hz || 1600 || the middle of the band
## code::filterWidth:: || 0.2 .. 9 oct || 3 || how wide the band is, in octaves
## code::level:: || -24 .. 12 dB || 0 || the repeats, in dB
## code::output:: || -36 .. 24 dB || 0 || the whole thing, in dB
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: intervalNames
the intervals by name.

METHOD:: gridNames
the slices by name.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: repeatNow
go now, whatever the interval says.

METHOD:: resync
the interval starts here.

METHOD:: sixteenth
a sixteenth at this tempo, in seconds.

METHOD:: intervalTime
the interval, in seconds.

METHOD:: sliceTime
a slice, in seconds, before gridVary.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\drums, { Stammer.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.002, 0.1) * WhiteNoise.ar(0.4 ! 2), \stammer) }).play;
b = Stammer(Ndef(\drums), \stammer);
b.gui;
b.preset = Stammer.presetNames.choose;
b.free; Ndef(\drums).clear;
::
